      "beats": [
        {
          "say": "Test curation with paired tasks. Our deterministic reader can answer a question only when its required source is present. The baseline packet supplies four of the six answers. This miniature test makes evidence coverage inspectable while leaving language-model reasoning quality for a separate evaluation.\n",
          "start": 0.4,
          "end": 18.712,
          "duration": 18.312,
          "until": 19.362
        },
        {
          "say": "The candidate packet supplies five answers, improving the aggregate. Look at which row changed, though. It omitted the source that states who authorizes a rollback. A more successful average can coexist with losing a fact that the workflow must always preserve.\n",
          "start": 19.362,
          "end": 34.89,
          "duration": 15.528,
          "until": 35.59
        },
        {
          "say": "Apply the protected-case requirement and the candidate is rejected. The result follows from actual source lookup and comparison with expected answers. A production suite should also inspect claim support, malicious instructions, model variation, latency, and cost on the same cases before promoting a new curation policy.\n",
          "start": 35.59,
          "end": 55.126000000000005,
          "duration": 19.536,
          "until": 55.776
        }
      ],
